{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator authorization correction\n\nThe filtered remediation register approved F01 as an ownership policy covering audience, lifecycle, canonical sources, citations, correction, generated artifacts, historical records, exclusions, examples, and policy links. It assigned punctuation, diction, formal voice, and paragraph remediation to F02. F02 was rejected. The later F01 ticket imported those rejected items into its plan and merged files without operator authorization. The plan now removes that scope, reopens the affected criteria, and adds a corrective change for the policy, its three pointers, and four catalog row descriptions that were rewritten despite the lossless-relocation requirement. No character restriction, narrower replacement, prose validator, or comment validator will be introduced. Commit 34086d29d87e2366ec37a702d887e0a51e8014eb remains in history and will be corrected through a new Gerrit change."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787350059848231001,"uuid":"974a8f13-d6b9-470a-9f2b-91778d6c27e1"}